fdm: epoll_wait() with the signal mask set around it on QNX (no epoll_pwait)

QNX's epoll emulation (libepoll) has epoll_wait() but no epoll_pwait().
foot keeps its signals blocked except while it waits, so that a signal
(SIGCHLD from the shell, SIGINT, SIGTERM ...) interrupts the wait. On QNX
set the wait mask with sigprocmask() around epoll_wait(); a signal that
arrives between the unmask and the wait has already set got_signal, which is
checked first, so it is not left pending until the next event. And where
epoll_pwait() returns EINTR for a signal, QNX's epoll_wait() can return events
as well: the signal handlers (SIGCHLD ends the terminal) then freed FD
handlers those events pointed to, and foot crashed on exit (SIGSEGV in
fdm_poll). Drop the events when a signal came in; they are level-triggered
and are reported again.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/fdm.c
+++ b/fdm.c
@@ -444,8 +444,30 @@ fdm_poll(struct fdm *fdm)
 
     struct epoll_event events[tll_length(fdm->fds)];
 
+#if defined(__QNX__)
+    /* QNX's epoll has no epoll_pwait(): unblock the signals around a plain
+     * epoll_wait(). A signal that arrives before the wait starts sets
+     * got_signal and is handled below without waiting. */
+    sigset_t qnx_old_mask;
+    sigprocmask(SIG_SETMASK, &fdm->sigmask, &qnx_old_mask);
+    int r = got_signal
+        ? (errno = EINTR, -1)
+        : epoll_wait(fdm->epoll_fd, events, tll_length(fdm->fds), -1);
+    int qnx_errno = errno;
+    sigprocmask(SIG_SETMASK, &qnx_old_mask, NULL);
+    /* epoll_pwait() returns EINTR when a signal arrives; QNX's epoll_wait()
+     * may return events as well. The signal handlers below can remove (and
+     * free) FD handlers those events point to: drop the events, as
+     * epoll_pwait() would -- they are level-triggered and come again. */
+    if (r > 0 && got_signal) {
+        r = -1;
+        qnx_errno = EINTR;
+    }
+    errno = qnx_errno;
+#else
     int r = epoll_pwait(
         fdm->epoll_fd, events, tll_length(fdm->fds), -1, &fdm->sigmask);
+#endif
 
     int errno_copy = errno;
 
